    "name": "RC HIIT (High Intensity Interval Training)",
    "text": "2\nRC HIIT (High Intensity Interval Training)\nInstructions\n\nTranslate the passage*\n\nRC HIIT Phase 1: Complete the following RC Thunderdome outputs in under 30 seconds each before beginning the questions. These outputs may require looking at the passage.\n\nOutline the structure of the passage overall.\n\nYou can use paragraphs as an organizing structure, but you can also delineate on a more fine-grained level, if desired.\n\nParallel one piece of the passage.\n\nPick an example, one line of reasoning, or a given person's point of view.\n\nSub out one word in the passage and replace it with a new word/phrase that means the same thing.\n\nPick one sentence out of the passage and identify its function.\n\nWhat is the Main Point?\n\nRC HIIT Phase 2: Complete the following RC Thunderdome outputs in under 30 seconds each. You have two options in how you complete the Phrase 2 outputs: You may complete all the additional RC Thunderdome outputs before beginning the questions or complete two to three additional RC Thunderdome outputs in between each of the questions. These outputs do not require you to look at the passage.\n\nWhat is the tone of the passage?\n\nWho is the author?\n\nWho is the audience?\n\nWho are the players in the passage and what do they believe?\n\nStrengthen the author's opinion\n\nIf the passage feels neutral, write a confirming piece of evidence for the information the author is presenting.\n\nWeaken the author's opinion\n\nIf the passage feels neutral, write a disconfirming piece of evidence for the information the author is presenting.\n\nOne Inference from the passage\n\nOne thing the author is likely to believe\n\nIdentify a principle underlying the passage as a whole or an argument within the passage\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
